####################################################################
# cat2a_process_priority.dlog — HAND-AUTHORED. NOT GENERATED.
#
# NL rule (CAT2, "simultaneous alarms likely carrying overlapping or
# redundant information"): "If an active alarm of equal or higher priority
# represents the same biological process of an incoming alarm, then the
# incoming alarm concerning that process can be silenced."
#
# Clause by clause (decisions agreed 2026-09-21):
#   "an incoming alarm"        — a PHYSIOLOGICAL alarm, at its arrival.
#                                Technical alarms that carry a metric
#                                (e.g. "SpO2 geen pols") report device
#                                state and are never silenced by CAT2a.
#   "an active alarm"          — a physiological alarm of the same patient
#                                whose transient graph is valid now, other
#                                than the incoming one.
#   "equal or higher priority" — priorityRank(active) >= priorityRank
#                                (incoming), priority_rank.ttl. An Unknown
#                                priority cannot be compared: an alarm with
#                                it is never silenced (skipped before the
#                                query) and never silences one.
#   "represents the same       — metric -> mda:approximates -> physiological
#    biological process"         property -> mda:isPropertyOf -> process,
#                                shared by both alarms. A property belonging
#                                to MORE than one process (ArterialPressure,
#                                TissuePerfusion: CardiacContraction and
#                                ArterialCirculation) matches only itself —
#                                otherwise a low MAP is hidden behind a
#                                bradycardia. Properties of a single process
#                                match each other (heart rate vs pulse rate).
#   "overlapping or redundant" — (from the category header) the incoming
#                                alarm deviates in the SAME direction as the
#                                active one and is NOT MORE SEVERE
#                                (metric_state_order.ttl): a reversal
#                                (tachycardia -> asystole) or an escalation
#                                (severe bradycardia -> asystole) is new
#                                information. The NL rule should read "...the
#                                same biological process, deviating in the
#                                same direction and not more severely...".
#   "can be silenced"          — for as long as an alarm that justified it
#                                at arrival is still active: the silence is
#                                stored (mdapoc:silencedBy, one link per
#                                justifying alarm, in the incoming alarm's
#                                transient graph) and LIFTED when the last of
#                                them ends while the incoming alarm is still
#                                active. Not expressible as a rule here; see
#                                replay_driver.py's cat2a_silence_insert and
#                                cat2a_lift.
#
# REPORTED STATE. Direction and severity come from the metric state
# (hasValueState or hasRhythm) matched INSIDE each alarm's own graph: the
# metric node is shared by every alarm on that pathway and can carry
# several states at once, but the copy in an alarm's own graph is the state
# that alarm reported. This relies on no alarm ever editing another's graph
# (last-wins removed 2026-09-21, replay_driver's module docstring); should
# last-wins return, this is where it would break.
#
# GRAPHS. ?gT is the incoming alarm's transient graph, ?gA an active
# alarm's; everything each alarm contributes is matched inside its own
# graph, so no hop is borrowed from another alarm. Priority rank, process
# membership and state order are static facts in the default graph.
#
# NOT LOADED AS A STANDING RULE. It runs as a one-shot `select` (and the
# silence INSERT) at each alarm's arrival, hand-translated into
# engine/replay_driver.py's _ONDEMAND_BODY_TEMPLATES["cat2a"]; the incoming
# alarm's priority is passed in there (it is inserted only after its own
# checks). It replaces the standing aggregate (shadow/
# cat2a_priority_aggregate.dlog, no longer loaded): the redundancy test
# compares direction, severity and priority of ONE active alarm at once,
# which per-key maxima cannot express. Negation is written in SPARQL form
# below (query-only), so this file documents the logic rather than being
# loadable Datalog. Keep the two in sync by hand; the cat2a_* fixtures check
# both.
####################################################################

@prefix mda:              <https://w3id.org/mda/ontology#> .
@prefix mdapoc:           <https://w3id.org/mda/poc#> .
@prefix alarmcat:         <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/alarm-category/> .
@prefix alarmprio:        <https://w3id.org/mda/vocab/alarm-priority/> .

[?alarm, mdapoc:silencedBy, ?active] ?gT :-
    # the incoming alarm (its own graph); ?incomingPrio passed in
    [?alarm, mda:hasCategory, alarmcat:Physiological] ?gT,
    [?alarm, mda:hasMessage, ?msg] ?gT,
    [?msg, mda:concernsPatient, ?patient] ?gT,
    [?analysis, mda:producesMetric, ?metric] ?gT,
    [?metric, mda:approximates, ?property] ?gT,
    [?metric, ?stateProp, ?state] ?gT,
    FILTER(?stateProp IN (mda:hasValueState, mda:hasRhythm)),
    [?property, mda:isPropertyOf, ?process],
    [?incomingPrio, mda:priorityRank, ?incomingRank],
    [?state, mdapoc:deviationDirection, ?direction],
    [?state, mdapoc:deviationSeverity, ?severity],
    # an active alarm of the same patient (its own graph)
    [?active, mda:hasCategory, alarmcat:Physiological] ?gA,
    [?active, mda:hasMessage, ?activeMsg] ?gA,
    [?activeMsg, mda:concernsPatient, ?patient] ?gA,
    [?active, mda:hasPriority, ?activePrio] ?gA,
    [?activeAnalysis, mda:producesMetric, ?activeMetric] ?gA,
    [?activeMetric, mda:approximates, ?activeProperty] ?gA,
    [?activeMetric, ?activeStateProp, ?activeState] ?gA,
    FILTER(?activeStateProp IN (mda:hasValueState, mda:hasRhythm)),
    [?activeProperty, mda:isPropertyOf, ?process],
    [?activePrio, mda:priorityRank, ?activeRank],
    [?activeState, mdapoc:deviationDirection, ?direction],
    [?activeState, mdapoc:deviationSeverity, ?activeSeverity],
    FILTER(?active != ?alarm),
    FILTER(?activePrio != alarmprio:Unknown),
    FILTER(?activeRank >= ?incomingRank),
    FILTER(?activeSeverity >= ?severity),
    # a property of more than one process matches only itself
    FILTER(?property = ?activeProperty || (
        NOT EXISTS { ?property mda:isPropertyOf ?p2 . FILTER(?p2 != ?process) } &&
        NOT EXISTS { ?activeProperty mda:isPropertyOf ?p3 . FILTER(?p3 != ?process) })) .

# VALIDATION — engine/replay_driver.py run(), fixtures in
# DATA/CAT_evaluation/events_data.csv: cat2a_pos (severe bradycardia, then
# bradycardia) and cat2a_gate (low MAP on two monitors) silence;
# cat2a_neg, cat2a_opposite, cat2a_escalation, cat2a_reversal, cat2a_hr_map,
# cat2a_technical and cat2a_unknown do not; cat2a_lift and cat2a_lift_last
# are silenced and lifted when the last justifying alarm ends.
